<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferns</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferns is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wexford">County Wexford</a>, Ireland, once the royal seat of the kings of Leinster of the Uí Cheinnselaig dynasty. A monastery was founded there by St Máedóc around 600, and it became the seat of a diocese. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a> ruled from Ferns, and after the Anglo-Norman invasion a large stone castle was built there in the 13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferns.jpg" alt="Ferns" width="320" height="529" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pratt, Anne; Pratt, Anne; Society for Promoting Christian Knowledge (Great Britain) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_ferns_of_Great_Britain,_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses,_pepperworts,_and_horsetails_(Pl._2)_(8515393495).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
